db2 get dbm cfg |grep -i FEDERATED

================================================================================================================================================================================================================
To check whether DB2 Federation is configured and available:
1. Check Federated Parameter
db2 get db cfg for <DBNAME> | grep -i federated

Example output:
Federated Database System Support (FEDERATED) = YES

2. Check Existing Wrappers
Connect to the database:
db2 connect to <DBNAME>

SELECT WRAPNAME, LIBRARY FROM SYSCAT.WRAPPERS;

Example:
DRDA
ORACLE

3. Check Federated Servers

SELECT SERVERNAME,
       WRAPNAME,
       SERVERTYPE,
       VERSION
FROM SYSCAT.SERVERS;

4. Check Nicknames

Nicknames are DB2 objects that point to remote Oracle tables.
SELECT TABSCHEMA,
       TABNAME
FROM SYSCAT.TABLES
WHERE TYPE='N';

Example:
FEDUSER  CUSTOMER_NK
FEDUSER  POLICY_NK

